# Fixture

PROVIDES fixture infrastructure
SO THAT node-status tests
CAN pin results of every verification type to read paths

## Assertions

### Scenarios

- Given a first input, when it is processed, then the first output is produced ([test](tests/first.scenario.l1.test.ts))
- Given a second input, when it is evaluated, then the second output is produced ([eval](evals/tests/second.scenario.l1.test.ts))
- Given a third input, when the running node is observed, then the third output is produced ([probe](probes/tests/third.scenario.l1.test.ts))

### Compliance

- ALWAYS: the first rule holds ([audit:rule-one])
